00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
hey what's up good folks this is dr john  delany with ramsey network  today we are talking about social  anxiety  got an email here we go  hi dr john what's up i have loved your  anxiety videos and wanted to ask you a  specific question  thank you i appreciate it i don't want  to sound tone deaf by saying covet has  been a good thing for me but the  shutdown cancelled  all social events that would ordinarily  cause me to have breakdowns and anxiety  attacks  it has been the most peaceful time of my  life even though i have been home with  six children because i haven't had to  see anyone except my family  last week sports reopened for our oldest  three children  i quickly started to feel tightness in  my chest and shoulders and i'm on edge  like never before  i'm scared to death of people and their  opinions will the other moms like me  will they think i'm too fat do they  notice that i always have my hair in a  messy bun  because i don't know how to do anything  else with it does she know my childhood  rapist and is she going to tell them  where i  am is the babies fussing annoying them  do they remember my family's history  here  and think i'm the same as the others  does she think i'm worthless for not  having a job and on and on  do you have any suggestions for anxiety  related to a person's own lack of  self-confidence and self-worth  and for dealing with anxiety attacks  that come from social interactions  susan thank you so much for your email  this is a lot  and i'm going to dig in here we go first  let's just define social anxiety right  it's a phobia or a fear of social  interactions  when you get around people when you get  around unfamiliar situations  your anxiety alarms go off and if you've  had trauma in your past  they go off loud for those of you who  don't have a social phobia you think  social anxiety is stupid it's not even  real so lame dude get over it  imagine yourself in a dark alley you  turn a corner  and there's three dudes with guns and  another dude with a knife and they start  running at you  how you would freeze your heart would  start racing your pupils dilate  and you go into full fight or flight  mode  or freeze mode that's social anxiety  when somebody goes to a grocery store  that's social anxiety when somebody  walks into church that's social anxiety  when somebody shows up to a little  league game  and they just want to support their kid  but every alarm system they have is  going off internally  and it just makes it hard to breathe  the author of this email susan she's  asking exposure questions  are people going to actually know me are  they going to see me  are they going to be judging the way i  look are they going to be judging my  inadequacies are they going to be  judging my blessings  the answer susan is no most people most  of the time  don't care about you you know why  because they're busy with their own  insecurities  they're worried about other people  watching them or some people are just  blessed and they simply don't care other  people think about them  what a gift that would be right some  people work really hard to get to that  place  or they had great parents great  community great social circles  that have built them up have given them  internal self-confidence they love  themselves  and they just radiate joy to other  people they don't really care what  people think about them  but most people most of the time are  worried how they present themselves to  the world  to other people know that my kids  sporting goods gear is used  the people know that my kid's not the  best player on the team and it's kind of  embarrassing  or that i didn't get to brush my teeth  today before i can't whatever people are  usually thinking about themselves  thinking about other people thinking  about them right  it's this toxic hurricane that we all  live in  so susan the answer really it's probably  not  and if people do notice wow she's more  overweight than we are  or her hair is messier than yours is who  cares  who cares you know why they don't get a  vote  they don't get a vote you're raising six  kids you have six kids the fact that  you're upright and breathing and they're  all fed  is more than most people will do in a  given day most  people cannot do what you do and that  leads me to number two  really the most revealing part of this  email  you mention a childhood rapist for me  that is stop the presses  that is park it right there we're not  going forward  until you have some coping mechanisms  for dealing with childhood trauma  severe childhood trauma that's a park it  until you've got  a community that's going to walk  alongside you until you've got some  uh support exercises some ways of being  to silence the alarms  because if you have severe childhood  trauma like childhood physical abuse or  sexual abuse childhood rape  social situations are ghastly  that part of your brain that is always  skinning the environment for future pain  for future hurt for future trauma  every time you get around strangers  every time you get around other people  that alarm's going off that alarm will  go off and go off and go off  you also discuss a family history here  that you don't want other people to know  about  maybe you've got family members in your  past maybe you've got family members who  left a poor legacy for you that you're  having to  live into as a member of the same  community that they lived in  again trauma can become legacy based  until you turn  with the right support and face it so a  link between  childhood adversity childhood trauma  childhood abuse and social anxiety  that link is clear as can be your brain  is on high alert  and it is always scanning the  environment for who's going to hurt me  next  so the real question susan you've got to  ask yourself is this  do you want to get to a place where you  can go out  do you want to go to these baseball  games and these church events  and the neighborhood grocery store  peaceful  light and fully engaged  and if you don't that's okay that's a  decision you're gonna make  right but if you do i want you know  there's healing on the other side of it  but the first thing you have to do is  make that decision  first thing you do have to answer that  question for yourself  right in your email you say this has  been the greatest few months of your  life  ask yourself do you want to be a person  who thrives in public  if you do if you want to be a person who  will  be out in public with her six kids that  will go to little league games and dance  recitals and 4-h events  or graduations and college send-offs  if you want to be that mom you will have  to invest  deeply in trauma-based trauma-focused  therapy  and that can look like emdr that can  look like brain spotting  that can look like tfc bt trauma focus  cognitive behavioral therapy  that looks like getting with someone who  is going to walk alongside you  teach you skills on how to silence the  alarms  skills on how to exhale when you feel  them coming up  go back through your trauma narrative  and teach you how to be safe moving  forward  susan if you want to be free from this  trauma  from this pain healing's out there it  truly is  my hope is my deepest hope and prayer  for you susan  is that you decide this past trauma  this social anxiety this weight that  sits on me all the time  i don't want that to be my identity  anymore  i want to walk towards peace  if you do healing's there there is a  counselor that will walk alongside you  and help you grow and heal from the  inside out  i want you to be whole and healed and no  longer looking around  for your childhood abuser a present  whole and joy-filled  mom for your six beautiful kids  they deserve that but more importantly  susan  you deserve that because you are worthy  of being  loved you are worthy of peace you are  worthy of a deep  good night sleep  you are worthy of going to your kid's  baseball game and cheering like a crazy  mama  and i hope you'll get that healing i  believe in you and i know you can do  this  this has been dr john dolone for ramsey  network if you know of somebody who's  dealing with social anxiety disorder  if you know somebody who's had childhood  abuse send them this video  don't forget to subscribe follow me at  johndaloni  and if you want to be on the dr john  deloney show  the live call-in show i want to hear  from you  email me at askjohn ramseysolutions.com  leave your cell number  a brief description of your question and  somebody from ramsey network will reach  out to you  and get a schedule to talk together i  can't wait take care

